                                "text": "In the year 1775, there stood upon the borders of Epping Forest, at a distance of about twelve miles from London—measuring from the Standard in Cornhill; or rather from the spot on or near to which the Standard used to be in days of yore — a house of public entertainment called the Maypole; […]",
